{"parentUuid":"35395cb4-9a4a-4bcc-8cab-e7824c1df98b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a096e9626858017f0","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CforS3jup8Q9Dvw7cMow6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five test runs are green, and no library/app code was touched — only the three specified test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":989,"cache_read_input_tokens":116391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":989,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"55ded92c-b774-458e-9dee-0a3b54831d4c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CforS3VXSdXN6yBV9nCr9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd252c02-88f7-40b3-bcbc-22e1378087ab","timestamp":"2026-10-08T00:51:01.506Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"fd252c02-88f7-40b3-bcbc-22e1378087ab","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a096e9626858017f0","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CforS3jup8Q9Dvw7cMow6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AtfvZHrsUfPwQQMoaPT9rW","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"All three target tests fixed and green, plus the two regression checks confirmed green. No library/app code changed — only the three test files.\n\nDiffs (brief):\n\n1. `mes-log-mcp/tests/check_compare.py`\n   - Added `_real_newest_clear(vin)` helper: independently re-walks `CATALOG.select(vin)` and checks each log's text against `mes.fes.CLEARING_RE` to find the newest clear-marked log (deliberately not calling `mes.verdict._last_clear` itself, to avoid a tautological test).\n   - Phase-2 check \"real newest_clear is the 2026-09-25 20:27 scan clear\" → now asserts `real[\"newest_clear\"] == _real_newest_clear(VIN)`.\n   - Updated the module docstring to drop the hardcoded dates.\n   - Left the ECM P0455/P0456/P0440 `logged_not_live` classification checks untouched — verified they still hold against the current 37-log corpus (newest clear 2026-09-29 10:46, newest ECM log is the 2026-10-04 11:16 FES session, which still shows no stored EVAP codes).\n\n2. `mes-log-mcp/tests/check_dashboard.py`\n   - Added `from mes.catalog import CATALOG`.\n   - \"log count matches the corpus (32 logs)\" → now computes `expected_log_count = len(CATALOG.select(vin=VIN))` (same call `analysis.vehicle_summary`/`dashboard.build` make) and asserts against that instead of a hardcoded 32.\n\n3. `cuore/tests/check_live_vs_log.py`\n   - Added a manual `sys.path` insert for `mes-log-mcp` (mirroring what `cuore.bootstrap` does) so the corpus can be inspected before any `cuore` import, plus imports of `CATALOG`/`CLEARING_RE`/`datetime`.\n   - Added `_real_newest_clear(vin)` (same independent-reimplementation approach as in check_compare.py).\n   - Added `_after_newest_log(vin)`: returns an ISO timestamp one day after the newest real log for the VIN (via `CATALOG.select(vin)[0].timestamp`).\n   - The synthetic live ECM P0455 observation's `\"at\"` is now `_after_newest_log(VIN)` instead of the hardcoded `\"2026-09-26T00:00:00\"` (which had fallen behind the new 2026-09-29/10-04 logs) — this keeps the fake read newer than the whole corpus, so it still classifies as `live_not_logged` rather than drifting into `logged_not_live`.\n   - \"newest_clear is the real 2026-09-25 20:27 scan clear\" → now asserts against `_real_newest_clear(VIN)`.\n   - Updated docstring accordingly.\n\nTest results:\n- `check_compare.py`: all checks passed (exit 0)\n- `check_dashboard.py`: all 40 checks passed (exit 0)\n- `check_live_vs_log.py`: 16 checks, 0 failures (exit 0)\n- `check_api.py`: 96 checks run, all green (exit 0)\n- `check_workup.py`: all checks passed (exit 0)\n\nAll five now self-correct as more real logs arrive, since the expected values are derived from the corpus (via `CATALOG`/`CLEARING_RE`) rather than pinned dates/counts."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":989,"cache_read_input_tokens":116391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":989,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AtfvZHrsUfPwQQMoaPT9rW":{"message":"All three target tests fixed and green, plus the two regression checks confirmed green. No library/app code changed — only the three test files.\n\nDiffs (brief):\n\n1. `mes-log-mcp/tests/check_compare.py`\n   - Added `_real_newest_clear(vin)` helper: independently re-walks `CATALOG.select(vin)` and checks each log's text against `mes.fes.CLEARING_RE` to find the newest clear-marked log (deliberately not calling `mes.verdict._last_clear` itself, to avoid a tautological test).\n   - Phase-2 check \"real newest_clear is the 2026-09-25 20:27 scan clear\" → now asserts `real[\"newest_clear\"] == _real_newest_clear(VIN)`.\n   - Updated the module docstring to drop the hardcoded dates.\n   - Left the ECM P0455/P0456/P0440 `logged_not_live` classification checks untouched — verified they still hold against the current 37-log corpus (newest clear 2026-09-29 10:46, newest ECM log is the 2026-10-04 11:16 FES session, which still shows no stored EVAP codes).\n\n2. `mes-log-mcp/tests/check_dashboard.py`\n   - Added `from mes.catalog import CATALOG`.\n   - \"log count matches the corpus (32 logs)\" → now computes `expected_log_count = len(CATALOG.select(vin=VIN))` (same call `analysis.vehicle_summary`/`dashboard.build` make) and asserts against that instead of a hardcoded 32.\n\n3. `cuore/tests/check_live_vs_log.py`\n   - Added a manual `sys.path` insert for `mes-log-mcp` (mirroring what `cuore.bootstrap` does) so the corpus can be inspected before any `cuore` import, plus imports of `CATALOG`/`CLEARING_RE`/`datetime`.\n   - Added `_real_newest_clear(vin)` (same independent-reimplementation approach as in check_compare.py).\n   - Added `_after_newest_log(vin)`: returns an ISO timestamp one day after the newest real log for the VIN (via `CATALOG.select(vin)[0].timestamp`).\n   - The synthetic live ECM P0455 observation's `\"at\"` is now `_after_newest_log(VIN)` instead of the hardcoded `\"2026-09-26T00:00:00\"` (which had fallen behind the new 2026-09-29/10-04 logs) — this keeps the fake read newer than the whole corpus, so it still classifies as `live_not_logged` rather than drifting into `logged_not_live`.\n   - \"newest_clear is the real 2026-09-25 20:27 scan clear\" → now asserts against `_real_newest_clear(VIN)`.\n   - Updated docstring accordingly.\n\nTest results:\n- `check_compare.py`: all checks passed (exit 0)\n- `check_dashboard.py`: all 40 checks passed (exit 0)\n- `check_live_vs_log.py`: 16 checks, 0 failures (exit 0)\n- `check_api.py`: 96 checks run, all green (exit 0)\n- `check_workup.py`: all checks passed (exit 0)\n\nAll five now self-correct as more real logs arrive, since the expected values are derived from the corpus (via `CATALOG`/`CLEARING_RE`) rather than pinned dates/counts."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"55ded92c-b774-458e-9dee-0a3b54831d4c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CforS3VXSdXN6yBV9nCr9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d1785671-5a69-4bf5-8f8f-ceeb87370d76","timestamp":"2026-10-08T00:51:13.120Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
